  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the integral <math><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#8747;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></math>.&nbsp;Then, which of the following is incorrect?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
